  "id": "Compound::DB01115 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Nifedipine is linked to Cyp2e1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the enzyme Cyp2a6 and Cyp2b6. These enzymes participate in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, an essential step in the biosynthesis of pro-inflammatory mediators. The observed pathway suggests that Nifedipine may influence the activity of these cytochrome P450 enzymes, potentially altering the metabolism of arachidonic acid and its downstream products. The presence of multiple pathways involving different Cyp2 subtypes highlights a broader role of these enzymes in lipid metabolism, with Cyp2e1 being a key participant in this process. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Cyp2e1 in the metabolic response to Nifedipine, suggesting a potential mechanism by which the drug affects enzyme activity and, consequently, lipid metabolism.",
